WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:24.680
- [Announcer] This is Sissel Tolaas.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.819
She is many things.

00:00:25.819 --> 00:00:27.679
An artist, a scientist,

00:00:27.679 --> 00:00:30.762
but more importantly, a smell expert.

00:00:31.611 --> 00:00:34.611
She, however, prefers another title.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:40.602
- [Announcer] Which means what, exactly?

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.699
- [Announcer] Right, the point is,

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:49.600
she's dedicated her life
to the sense of smell,

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.461
what it means, and how it can be used

00:00:51.461 --> 00:00:54.711
to understand the world and each other.

00:01:16.685 --> 00:01:17.917
- [Announcer] So how
exactly did she go about

00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:19.724
recording and then reproducing

00:01:19.724 --> 00:01:20.807
these smells?

00:01:54.157 --> 00:01:55.898
- [Announcer] Name a city,
a neighborhood within

00:01:55.898 --> 00:01:57.477
a neighborhood, a
historical building, or even

00:01:57.477 --> 00:02:00.829
an era in time, and most
likely Sissel has reproduced

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:03.567
that smell, along with
thousands of other scents

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:06.887
here in her lab, with the
hopes of using the findings

00:02:06.887 --> 00:02:08.637
for a bigger purpose.

